IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssa-common`
IMPORT `ssa-figures`
IMPORT `ssa-title-xvi`
IMPORT `ssa-medicare`
IMPORT `ssa-seat`

-- Social Security Act -- worked cases for the SSI applicant (Title XVI) and for Medicare enrollment.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from
-- the deposited text and the 2026 figures (90 FR 49047: $994 / $1,491; 90 FR 52063: $202.90), never copied from the
-- encoding's output. All people are HYPOTHETICAL. Amounts are monthly.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1382c(a)(1): aged, blind, or disabled. 66, resident citizen: yes. 40, neither blind nor disabled: no. 40 and disabled:
-- yes. 70 and not a resident: no.
#ASSERT `Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` 66 FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` 40 TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an aged, blind, or disabled individual` 70 FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1382a: countable income in 2026. Inputs: earned, unearned, need-based (non-State) part, student, student exclusion used,
-- work expenses, blind.
-- Jo's only income is $800 of Social Security: less the $20 general exclusion, $780.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 0 800 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 780
-- Earnings of $1,000 and nothing else: the $20 goes to earnings, then $65, then half: ($1,000 - $85) / 2 = $457.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 1000 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 457.5
-- $500 unearned and $1,000 earned: $480 + ($1,000 - $65) / 2 = $480 + $467.50 = $947.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 1000 500 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 947.5
-- $300 of a needs-based pension (not State aid) is not reduced by the $20 (s 1382a(b)(2)(A)); with no earnings it is
-- unused: $300.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 0 300 300 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 300
-- With $100 of earnings as well, the $20 comes off them: $300 + ($100 - $20 - $65) / 2 = $300 + $7.50 = $307.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 100 300 300 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 307.5
-- A student under 22 earning $3,000: $2,410 excluded (s 1382a(b)(1)), then $20, $65, half: ($590 - $85) / 2 = $252.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 3000 0 0 TRUE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 252.5
-- With $9,000 already excluded this year, only $730 is left of the $9,730: ($3,000 - $730 - $85) / 2 = $1,092.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 3000 0 0 TRUE 9000 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 1092.5
-- Disabled, $1,000 earned, $100 impairment-related work expenses before the half: ($915 - $100) / 2 = $407.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 1000 0 0 FALSE 0 100 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 407.5
-- Blind, $1,000 earned, $100 work expenses after the half: $915 / 2 - $100 = $357.50.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2026 1000 0 0 FALSE 0 100 TRUE EQUALS `answered` 357.5
-- 2025: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my countable income for SSI` 2025 1000 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1382(a), (b): the SSI benefit for a month of 2026. Inputs: year, age, blind, disabled, resident, eligible spouse, deeming
-- case, living arrangement, earned, unearned, need-based part, student, student used, work expenses, resources other than
-- home, excluded resources.
-- Jo, 70, own household, $800 Social Security, $1,500 in the bank: $994 - $780 = $214.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 800 0 FALSE 0 0 1500 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 214
-- No income at all: the full $994.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 1500 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 994
-- Kim, 45 and disabled, earning $1,000: $994 - $457.50 = $536.50.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 45 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 1000 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 536.5
-- A couple, both aged, $1,000 of Social Security between them, $2,500 of resources (within $3,000): $1,491 - $980 = $511.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `in my own household` 0 1000 0 FALSE 0 0 2500 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 511
-- The couple living in another's household on in-kind support: the rate is cut by a third, $1,491 x 2/3 = $994; with $494
-- of Social Security: $994 - $474 = $520.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `in another person's household, receiving support and maintenance in kind from that person` 0 494 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 520
-- Jo with $2,500 of resources: over $2,000. With $5,000 of which $4,000 is her car (excluded): $1,000, within.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 800 0 FALSE 0 0 2500 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "resources over the limit (s 1382(a)(1)(B), (a)(3))"
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 800 0 FALSE 0 0 5000 4000 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 214
-- Social Security of $1,100: countable $1,080, above $994: none.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 1100 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "countable income above the benefit rate (s 1382(a)(1)(A))"
-- In a nursing home all month with Medicaid paying: $30 ($360 a year); with $40 of income ($20 countable): $10.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `throughout the month in a medical treatment facility, with Medicaid paying for my care` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 30
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `throughout the month in a medical treatment facility, with Medicaid paying for my care` 0 40 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 10
-- An inmate of a public institution all month: not eligible.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `throughout the month an inmate of a public institution` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "an inmate of a public institution throughout the month is not an eligible individual (s 1382(e)(1)(A))"
-- 40, not blind or disabled: not an aged, blind, or disabled individual.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "not an aged, blind, or disabled individual (s 1382c(a)(1))"
-- Living with an ineligible spouse: deeming, not covered. A couple in a medical facility: not covered. 2027: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `in my own household` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `benefit not covered` `deeming of an ineligible spouse's or parent's income and resources (s 1382c(f)) is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2026 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `throughout the month in a medical treatment facility, with Medicaid paying for my care` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `benefit not covered` `the reduced rate in a medical treatment facility is encoded only for an individual without an eligible spouse`
#ASSERT `How much SSI can I get` 2027 70 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `in my own household` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `benefit not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1382(c)(7): an application filed 10 March 2026 by someone already eligible takes effect 1 April 2026. One who becomes
-- eligible on 20 May 2026: 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `From which month does my SSI application take effect` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 4
#ASSERT `From which month does my SSI application take effect` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 20 5 2026) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 6
-- A December filing takes effect the next January.
#ASSERT `From which month does my SSI application take effect` (Date 10 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2027, `month` IS 1

-- s 1383(e)(2): reductions for reports not made or late: $25, $50, $100, and none without fault or with good cause.
#ASSERT `How much is my SSI reduced for a late report` 1 FALSE EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `How much is my SSI reduced for a late report` 2 FALSE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `How much is my SSI reduced for a late report` 4 FALSE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `How much is my SSI reduced for a late report` 1 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- The regulative rule, with a HYPOTHETICAL 10 days set by the Commissioner: a report on day 5 fulfils it.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 1383(e) -- the SSI recipient must report events and changes in circumstances as the Commissioner requires` 10) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `report the event or change in circumstances` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the individual, "s 1383(e)(2)(A): ..." (no report in the 10 days)
#TRACE (`s 1383(e) -- the SSI recipient must report events and changes in circumstances as the Commissioner requires` 10) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)

-- s 1382(e)(2): notice dated 10 March 2026 that she may get a pension: steps to apply by 9 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for the other benefit` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 9 4 2026
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 1382(e)(2) -- after notice, the applicant must take all appropriate steps to apply for other payments within 30 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `take all appropriate steps to apply for and obtain the other payments` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the individual, "s 1382(e)(2): ..." (no steps within 30 days)
#TRACE `s 1382(e)(2) -- after notice, the applicant must take all appropriate steps to apply for other payments within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- s 1383(c): a hearing request within 60 days; the Commissioner's determination within 90 days of it (no disability issue).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 1383(c)(1) -- the applicant may request a hearing within 60 days after notice of the determination is received` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `request a hearing on the determination` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 1383(c)(2) -- the Commissioner must decide within 90 days of a hearing request that does not involve disability` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner of Social Security` `make the determination on the basis of the hearing` 80)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Commissioner of Social Security, "s 1383(c)(2): ..." (nothing decided by day 90)
#TRACE `s 1383(c)(2) -- the Commissioner must decide within 90 days of a hearing request that does not involve disability` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 91)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 426(a): Lee, born 15 July 1961, attains 65 in July 2026. On Social Security benefits: Part A in July 2026, not in June.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 15 7 1961) 2026 7 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 15 7 1961) 2026 6 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not yet on benefits but fully insured: only once he applies for Part A.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 15 7 1961) 2026 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 15 7 1961) 2026 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Born 1 July 1961: attains 65 on 30 June 2026 (finding 1), so entitled in June 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 1 7 1961) 2026 6 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not insured on any record and no government work: not entitled, but may buy Part A if enrolled in Part B.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to Part A at 65` (Date 15 7 1961) 2026 8 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can I buy Part A` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I buy Part A` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I buy Part A` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 1395o(a): eligible for Part B if entitled to Part A, or 65 and a resident citizen (or 5-year permanent resident).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to enroll in Part B` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to enroll in Part B` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible to enroll in Part B` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible to enroll in Part B` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- s 1395p(d): Lee's initial enrollment period: April 2026 to October 2026. Born 1 July 1961 (65 in June 2026): March to
-- September 2026.
#ASSERT `When does my Part B initial enrollment period begin` (Date 15 7 1961) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 4
#ASSERT `When does my Part B initial enrollment period end` (Date 15 7 1961) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 10
#ASSERT `When does my Part B initial enrollment period begin` (Date 1 7 1961) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 3
#ASSERT `When does my Part B initial enrollment period end` (Date 1 7 1961) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 9
-- s 1395p(e): January to March is a general enrollment period; April is not.
#ASSERT `is in a general enrollment period` (`the month number of` 2028 3)
#ASSERT NOT (`is in a general enrollment period` (`the month number of` 2028 4))
-- s 1395p(f): deemed enrolled if eligible through Part A, initial period after March 1973, living in the US outside Puerto
-- Rico.
#ASSERT `is deemed enrolled in Part B` TRUE (`the month number of` 2026 4) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is deemed enrolled in Part B` TRUE (`the month number of` 2026 4) FALSE)

-- s 1395q(a): when Lee's Part B coverage begins (first eligible July 2026).
-- Enrolling in May 2026, before July: July 2026. In July: August. In October, the last month of the period: November.
#ASSERT `From which month am I covered by Part B` `enrolled in the initial enrollment period` 2026 7 2026 5 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 7
#ASSERT `From which month am I covered by Part B` `enrolled in the initial enrollment period` 2026 7 2026 7 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 8
#ASSERT `From which month am I covered by Part B` `enrolled in the initial enrollment period` 2026 7 2026 10 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 11
-- Deemed enrolled in June 2026, the third month of the period (on benefits already): July 2026.
#ASSERT `From which month am I covered by Part B` `deemed enrolled` 2026 7 2026 6 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 7
-- Enrolling in the general enrollment period in February 2028: March 2028.
#ASSERT `From which month am I covered by Part B` `enrolled in a general enrollment period` 2026 7 2028 2 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2028, `month` IS 3

-- s 1395r: the 2026 premium. On time: $202.90. Enrolled in the general period ending March 2029 after his initial period
-- ended October 2026: 29 months, 2 full years: +20%, $243.48. If 20 of those months were in employer coverage from current
-- work: 9 months, no full year: $202.90. Enrolled in an s 1395p(i)(4) special period: no increase. 2027: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my Part B premium` 2026 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 202.9
#ASSERT `What is my Part B premium` 2026 29 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 243.48
#ASSERT `What is my Part B premium` 2026 29 20 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 202.9
#ASSERT `What is my Part B premium` 2026 29 0 TRUE EQUALS `answered` 202.9
#ASSERT `What is my Part B premium` 2027 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`
-- The permissions to enroll: in month 5 of the initial period; in month 6 after employer coverage ends.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 1395p(d) -- the individual may enroll in Part B during the seven-month initial enrollment period` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `enroll in Part B` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 1395p(i) -- after employer group health coverage ends, the individual may enroll in Part B within eight months` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `enroll in Part B` 6)) EQUALS FULFILLED
